man\npay (37 U.S.C. 203(c)) are set forth on Schedule 8 attached hereto and\nmade a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"64 FR 72237 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4","sha256":"6ecb44b776e7bbc76543f9bd398a15ad5d2fd2415de089c17e2c4749dca4c329","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1999-12-23/pdf/99-33511.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13144#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 5304\nof title 5, United States Code, and in accordance with section 646(a) of\nthe Treasury and General Government Appropriations Act, 2000, Public\nLaw 106–58, locality-based comparability payments shall be paid in accord-\nance with Schedule 9 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"64 FR 72237 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"6ecb44b776e7bbc76543f9bd398a15ad5d2fd2415de089c17e2c4749dca4c329","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1999-12-23/pdf/99-33511.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13144#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall take such\nactions as may be necessary to implement these payments and to publish\nappropriate notice of such payments in the Federal Register.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"64 FR 72237 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"6ecb44b776e7bbc76543f9bd398a15ad5d2fd2415de089c17e2c4749dca4c329","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1999-12-23/pdf/99-33511.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13144#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Administrative Law Judges. The rates of basic pay for administrative\nlaw judges, as adjusted under 5 U.S.C. 5372(b)(4), are set forth on Schedule\n10 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"64 FR 72238 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 6","sha256":"6ecb44b776e7bbc76543f